      "side": 1,
      "message": "Addressed in patch set 14: the single post-clear re-read is replaced by _settle_pending_bootmode(), which polls the pending value and re-clears once (bounded by the new bootmode_clear_attempts class attribute) before giving up, so a BIOS job that re-stages the value right after the clear no longer aborts the rebuild on the first disagreement. test_restaged_pending_bootmode_is_cleared_again covers the converge-on-second-attempt path (conflict, clear, conflict again, clear, clean -\u003e move proceeds), and test_conflicting_pending_bootmode_aborts now pins the two clear attempts before the abort. Mutation checked - collapsing the settle poll back to a single re-read fails the new test.\n\nI kept it bounded rather than folding it into the _wait_for_bootmode deadline loop: this path runs before anything is staged, so a genuinely stuck pending value should still surface quickly instead of consuming the 600s budget that the post-reboot wait needs.",
